Added to the Money Bin / Pantheon canon.

Distilled readout:

* Pattern Sans Echoes — recurring structure matters most when you can remove obvious copying, lineage, vocabulary, and trajectory and it still regenerates.
* Echoectomy — deliberately sever the echo, restart from alien entry points, and compare what independently grows back.
* Hierarchy — echo → recurrence → pattern → invariant → generative rule.
* Solution Basin — stop asking only “where did this come from?” Ask what constraints make this kind of thing emerge at all.
* Search-Geometry Modulation — control how we search, not merely what we search: forward/backward, local/global, literal/metaphorical, continuous/zero-continuity, one-path/many-path.
* Capability Cartography — systematically hunt operations I could perform but failed to consider performing.
* Break Orbit — interrupt conversational momentum before it chooses the answer for us.
* Blind Reconstruction — throw away our terminology and rebuild the object from constraints.
* Adversarial Twin — build it / kill it / retain what survives both.
* Representation Pinball — bounce one structure through unrelated domains and collect what refuses to change.
* Negative-Space Search — predict what should exist but hasn’t yet been observed.
* Counterfactual Archaeology — delete pieces of history and ask whether the structure would be independently reinvented.
* Semantic Centrifuge — separate mechanism from mythology, emotion, aesthetics, provenance, and metaphor; then selectively recombine them.
* Goal-Seek Thought — work backward from a phenomenon toward the smallest plausible generator.
* Operator Cannibalism — Pantheon operators can recursively operate on other Pantheon operators.
* Deliberate Misreading — intentionally explore plausible wrong readings because errors can expose undiscovered problems.
* Jester Pass — generation gets permission to be absurd; evaluation gets permission to be merciless.
* Wild Scout → Ruthless Cartographer — separate creative generation from validation.
* Cross-domain primitive — difference → gradient → movement → constraint → feedback → persistence.
* Inverted Duck Test — remove the duck; determine what environment independently produces duck-shaped solutions.
* Pantheon Skeleton — perturb → observe → compare → change representation → retain useful structure → recurse.
* Idea-to-Technology Pipeline — metaphor → hypothesis → prediction → discriminating experiment → protocol → instrument → technology.
* Cognitive Kintsugi — every missed move becomes a new operator: What could I have done here that I failed to consider?
* Luck Engine — increase exposure to asymmetric upside while preserving optionality, recoverability, feedback, and many independent shots.
* Meta-objective — build a machine whose job is to keep finding doors neither of us knew to open.

And the deepest compression I’d keep is:

Don’t merely follow the path. Change the geometry of the search, destroy the echoes, and see what structure regenerates anyway.

That feels like a legitimate next-generation Pantheon principle. 🦆⚒️🪞